{
  "0": "Interaction mechanism: across all four datasets, introduce jointly learned diagonal bilinear compatibility, s(h,i)=sum_d h_d*(1+0.1*tanh(a_d))*e_i,d, initializing a=0. This bounded adjustment may improve compatibility while retaining the initial scorer. Preserve the GRU, features, history readout, loss and optimizer; train and load one model per category, updating the predictor writer consistently.",
  "1": "Training strategy: across all four datasets, halve the current learning rate while preserving the optimizer, batch size, scheduler, regularization and stopping rules. Smaller updates may reduce the validation fluctuations and early deterioration seen in Electronics. Keep architecture, scoring, loss, seeds, splits and the 200-epoch cap fixed; retain one model per category.",
  "2": "Feature construction: across all four datasets, multiply each nonpadding input embedding by 1+0.1*min(log1p(c),log(4))/log(4), where c counts earlier occurrences of that item in the available history prefix. This bounded, causal repeat indicator may expose persistent interests without adding embedding dimensions or an independent scorer. Preserve embeddings, GRU topology, readout, loss and optimizer; reproduce the feature in inference with one model per category.",
  "3": "Interest aggregation: across all four datasets, replace the current history vector r with 0.9*r+0.1*m, where m pools existing valid GRU states with normalized weights proportional to 2^(-age/5). The small recency-weighted contribution may retain recent interests that the current readout misses while limiting disruption. Preserve history selection, embeddings, GRU, scoring, loss and optimizer; use this same readout in training and the generated predictor, with one model per category."
